WEBVTT

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:12.950
Shukoh...

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:19.040
Shukoh...

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:23.750
Shukoh...

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.910
Shukoh...

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:39.660
It's not uncommon to see students skipping class
on the rooftop in manga and such,

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:45.000
but if you actually took a nap up there,
you'd get a sunburn like no other.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.620
I think third period is about
to start for everyone else.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.910
I pretty much always skipped classes,

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.620
and Adachi rarely ever came to school.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.330
We happened to meet up here by chance,

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:00.660
and ended up spending a lot of time together.

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:05.040
Do you mind if I serve next?

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.450
Sure?

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.540
Huh?

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:13.120
What?!

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:16.370
I found out how to do that serve online.

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:20.700
But I didn't have a racket at home,
so I practiced with a rice paddle.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.330
No fair using curveballs on amateurs like me.

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.120
You lack ambition, young Shimamura.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.410
And that's not my... fault!

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.080
When we're skipping class like this,

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:41.040
--we can usually sense if the other is here.
--I can only get it to work like
one out of ten times right now.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.500
--And we usually find each other up here.
--So you're getting worse...

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.160
Let's do this!

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:51.790
I guess third period was PE class.

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:55.040
What if they come up here?

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.950
Why don't we open the windows and jump?

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.450
What?! But we're on the second floor!

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:02.500
Wouldn't we break our legs?

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.080
Ah, I see that you lack calcium in your diet.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:10.080
I really don't like that interpretation.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:19.330
Crap. This is sorta exciting.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:28.370
I don't think they realize
we're up here, though.

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:35.080
Maybe I'll just drink some milk
with my lunch today.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:38.080
So my legs don't break if we ever have to jump.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:45.080
I see. So you've decided
to strengthen your bones.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.120
This time we spent together
where nothing else mattered

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.950
always felt so nice.

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:29.620
Shukoh... Shukoh...

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:32.500
Shukoh...

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:39.870
Ugh, I can't anymore.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.330
It's so hot!

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:43.040
Wanna go outside?

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:45.250
It's almost lunchtime anyway.

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:51.290
My, how lewd. Our school's...

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.870
Um...

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:55.290
Dignity?

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:58.330
Yeah, that! Our school's dignity
is at stake here.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:03.200
It's lunchtime, but what should I do?

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:09.160
Yeah, yeah. We can't have you
go out in that state.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.160
I'll just go.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.410
I'll go next time.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:18.660
You and I always seem to have
different opinions about "next time."

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:25.160
Oh, you probably want your usual danish,

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:27.750
but do you want milk today?

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:29.160
Water, please.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.500
Roger.

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:33.410
Hup.

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:37.660
Doing bad things with Adachi is pretty fun.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:40.250
Is it because I got hooked
doing this with Adachi,

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:44.580
or do I just get a rush doing bad things?

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:46.500
The answer's obvious, but...

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.660
I'll leave things ambiguous for now.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.950
What is she even doing?

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:02.250
Shimamura was the first one to be up here
on the second floor of the gymnasium.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:06.910
She still looked like a middle schooler,

00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:11.830
so I figured she was a first-year like me.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:14.580
A-Adachi, was it?

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.160
Yeah?

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:20.750
Um, we're in the same class.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:23.250
Oh, right.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:25.660
My nickname's Shimamura, but in hiragana.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:27.750
Shimamura...

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:32.160
Do you come here often?

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:35.500
I just happened to stop by today.
What about you?

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.250
Pretty much the same.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:46.160
They're so loud.

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:47.290
Right?

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:58.790
Hiyah!

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:01.120
Oh.

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:08.700
Are you able to touch them?

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.750
Cicadas aren't too bad.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.160
Think it'll stay on?

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:27.580
How many days do you think it has left?

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:29.200
I dunno.

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:30.290
Yeah...

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:35.040
How much longer do you want it to live?

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:42.540
Fifteen days... I think.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:46.500
Fifteen days later,

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:50.660
Shimamura's hands were covered in dirt
when she came up to the second floor.

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:54.580
That was my first encounter with Shimamura.

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:55.540
Adachi!

00:07:56.950 --> 00:08:00.080
I got you the last danish.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.620
Here's your water.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:02.790
Thanks.

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:07.250
This was still when

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:10.620
I didn't consider Shimamura my friend yet.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:20.290
"Tea"

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.040
Squeak, squeak, squeak, squeak.

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:25.660
Pshuu.

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:30.540
"Learning Table Tennis From Zero"

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:35.120
I guess they have a book for everything.
Dang, that's expensive.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.660
Hey, it's Shimamura.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:38.830
Hino.

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:40.700
Whatcha lookin' at?

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.040
--Smash! You joining the table
tennis club, Shimamura?

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:44.700
--Hino is a classmate
who's sort of a plain jane.
--Smash! You joining the table
tennis club, Shimamura?

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:45.580
--Hino is a classmate
who's sort of a plain jane.
--No, I was just curious.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:47.500
--She's never even dyed her hair before.
--No, I was just curious.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.950
--She's never even shoplifted, either.
--Curious? You randomly picked
a book about ping-pong?

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:53.410
--She's apparently never pulled the hair
of a girl from another school, either.
--Curious? You randomly picked
a book about ping-pong?

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:54.500
Hey!

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:57.000
--Jeez. You just leave me behind
and end up finding Shimamura.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:01.200
--My other classmate, Nagafuji, is your
usual bespectacled girl with big boobs.
--Jeez. You just leave me behind
and end up finding Shimamura.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.620
--Need I say more?
--Jeez. You just leave me behind
and end up finding Shimamura.

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:04.290
--Need I say more?
--So, what were you
talking about?

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:08.000
--Her big boobs and her big attitude
make her pretty mature...
--Nothing important.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:08.620
--All right. I won't inquire any further then.

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:10.950
--...but she's a bit dumb.
--All right. I won't inquire any further then.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:16.000
Hino, do you have an excuse
for that blatant sexual harassment?

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.870
Nagafuji is too self-conscious,

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:20.950
so I thought I'd lighten the mood.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.410
Really?

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:26.290
Well, when they're this big,
the boys always look.

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:28.040
Of course, I'm self-conscious.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:31.120
I'm sure all the boys in class
staring at your boobies

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:34.200
have fondled them at least
ten times in their minds.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:38.160
What?! That's gross.

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:40.750
That's the price you pay for being famous.

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:42.580
Oh, whoops. My hand slipped.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:48.290
Apparently, Hino and Nagafuji
have been friends since they were little.

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:51.200
I became friends with them
after we got into high school,

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:54.450
so my distance with them varies.

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:57.120
But when it comes to distance,

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:00.950
being as close as you can be
isn't always the best option.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:05.750
If you get too close, you might fight
and have misunderstandings.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:10.700
Oh, yeah. The other day at the fishing hole
there was someone in a spacesuit...

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.330
Hey, look over there!

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:44.250
I think relationships with others

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:46.370
are like free diving.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:27.160
Hey, who was that?
Wasn't she in our class in like April?

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:31.290
You say that like every time we see her.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.450
Her name is Adachi.

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:34.790
She's our classmate.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:38.080
She's definitely a certified delinquent.
Teacher-approved.

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:39.500
Huh...?

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:41.080
Is she one of yours, Shimamura?

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:42.750
Who knows?

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:47.540
You keep sinking deeper and deeper,

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:51.080
and things start disappearing around you.

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:55.500
You struggle to breathe, so you try
to get back to the water's surface.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:03.870
And then you poke your head out
for a breath of air

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:06.200
before sinking deeper yet again.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:10.290
If you keep repeating that cycle...

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:20.580
Morning.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:28.620
Adachi...

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:30.950
Hey, you're late today.

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:33.160
Oh, I...

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:35.370
...thought I'd just head home,

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:39.080
but I heard the sound of a ping-pong ball.

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:42.700
I saw you yesterday.

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:44.580
Yeah, you did.

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:45.910
Where's your school bag?

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:48.290
In my bicycle's basket.

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:49.660
I see.

00:12:57.750 --> 00:12:59.290
Well, I'm heading home.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:01.950
Okay...

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:07.870
Say, Adachi.

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:14.750
"Let's go to class today,"

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:14.750
or "Let's walk home together today."

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:16.120
Which would you prefer?

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:19.750
Huh? Um...

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:28.040
In that case... I'll just go kill some time
somewhere until school's over... I guess.

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:32.250
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:38.370
You didn't have to be sitting
the same exact way.

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:40.790
Sorry, it started raining.

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:44.250
Well, the rain's not your fault.

00:13:44.250 --> 00:13:46.700
Which way is your house, Shimamura?

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:48.330
This way.

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:50.000
Oh, I thought so.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:53.500
Here, hold this.

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:57.830
I just figured your house
was pretty far from mine.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:13:59.620
I live this way.

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:04.370
So, whose home
should we go home to first?

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:06.410
That's a novel way of putting it.

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:11.450
Then... Why don't we go to your place first?

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:12.620
Okay.

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:18.950
Riding a bike like this is a crime, you know?

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:21.200
Like that matters. We're delinquents.

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:22.830
Good point.

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:25.660
Man, being delinquents rules.

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:27.620
It sure does.

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:35.200
So I guess you actually have friends.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:36.500
Huh?

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:39.250
Oh, you mean Hino and Nagafuji?

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:46.160
I thought you were always up there
because you didn't have friends.

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:47.370
What about you, Adachi?

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:49.000
Do you have friends?

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:53.080
You're probably my only one.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.450
That's so sad!

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:06.410
Killing time outside of school
and then going home together is weird.

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:08.660
This is definitely weird,

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:13.290
but the idea sounded amusing and elating.

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:16.450
If either of us were actually
honor students, we'd say,

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:19.200
"We shouldn't be doing this!"

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:24.160
And try to steer the other back down
the right path with the power of friendship,

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:27.700
but we were both pretty irresponsible.

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:30.700
So we were just dragging
each other down deeper.

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:37.500
So I go through here, and then...
to get back to my house...

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:39.370
That's a pretty decent walk.

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:41.040
Shimamura!

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.580
Here, I got you a towel.

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:46.950
Huh? Wh-Whoa.

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:48.870
Thanks.

00:15:48.870 --> 00:15:49.790
Sorry.

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:51.660
Huh? About what?

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:55.450
I feel bad for making you take
a really long way home.

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:58.000
Want me to give you a ride home?

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:01.290
Huh? No. This whole ride
would be pointless, then.

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:03.000
I guess you have a point.

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:09.950
Okay, I'm going home.

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:12.830
Yeah, I'll probably see you tomorrow.

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:18.500
When I looked down at Adachi's head
from the back of her bicycle,

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:22.080
I noticed her hair that usually
looked so pretty with her face

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:24.870
also looked like some floofy creature.

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:27.370
Maybe I looked the same way.

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:30.700
What a weird day.

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:48.580
See? I told you there were noises
coming from upstairs.

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:53.750
Huh? I guess you really were
playing table tennis.

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:55.290
Gack.

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:58.370
Did you really say, "Gack" to your friend?

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.620
Shimamura...

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:11.660
Adachi...

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:14.580
So, how'd you know I was here?

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:17.250
You were looking at the table tennis
book at the bookstore.

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:18.750
Whoopsie.

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:22.660
So... Is that Adachi over there?

00:17:22.660 --> 00:17:27.450
Um... I think that's pretty
self-explanatory, but yeah.

00:17:27.450 --> 00:17:29.620
Yup, Adachi.

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:32.500
You guys were friends?

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:34.450
Well, yeah.

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:39.000
Then yesterday... Well, whatever.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:40.330
I'm Nagafuji.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.200
I'm Hino.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:46.540
Nagafuji and Hino... Got it.

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:47.540
Nice to meet you.

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:50.580
Um... I bought us some bread.

00:17:50.580 --> 00:17:54.040
I'm surprised they never found
you guys during PE class.

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:57.040
We stayed pretty quiet
whenever there was class.

00:17:58.540 --> 00:18:01.040
Which one do you want, Adachi?

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:04.450
I'll take whichever one you like, Shimamura.

00:18:04.450 --> 00:18:07.540
Hm... In that case... Here!

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:12.830
Are you free on Sunday, Shimamura?

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:14.950
This week? I think so.

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:17.120
Then wanna go to the fishing hole?

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:21.160
That kid in the spacesuit
I was telling you about is a riot.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:24.870
Are you basically just asking me
to go fishing with you?

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:27.500
No, no. That's just a bonus.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:31.160
They said they wanted to meet you
when I mentioned you.

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:35.370
Why don't you just take Nagafuji with you?

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:37.040
I have club.

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:39.700
Come on, let's go!

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:41.620
Hm... Yeah, sure.

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:43.250
Heck yes!

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:45.910
Okay, we're going to the fishing hole on Sunday.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:51.000
The next day, Adachi didn't come here.

00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:57.410
There was a lot
I didn't know about Adachi,

00:18:57.410 --> 00:19:00.660
and that frustrated me at times.

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:06.580
What I did know was what I felt.

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:13.080
After seeing Hino and Nagafuji having
a blast up here yesterday, I realized again...

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:15.620
That's not what I wanted.

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:22.200
Adachi might not show up again for a while.

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:27.250
If I was super unlucky, I may not
see her again until graduation.

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:28.620
That was totally possible.

00:19:35.910 --> 00:19:39.410
I guess my luck does suck. Welp...

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:40.620
Blammo!

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:46.080
Huh?

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:48.830
A-Adachi?

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:50.540
Sorry...

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:55.120
I was planning to stop
but didn't make it in time.

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:57.790
I'm pretty sure I heard you say, "Blammo."

00:19:58.910 --> 00:20:00.540
Wait, are you sure about this?

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:01.700
About what?

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:04.290
Well, your house isn't this way.

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:05.910
Yeah, but...

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:08.040
Yeah, you're right.

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:12.410
Shimamura, here.

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:15.200
Huh? Wait, what?

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:17.250
"Eggy Bread"

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:20.830
I was going to give them
to you during lunch today.

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:22.000
Lunch?

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:23.910
Oh, so this is "next time."

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:28.250
I'm glad you weren't going home
with your other friends.

00:20:28.250 --> 00:20:30.540
I wouldn't have been able
to give them to you.

00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:37.160
What?

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:38.500
Oh, nothing.

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:44.040
Adachi had said that I was her only friend.

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:46.750
I guess that's all there is to it then.

00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:48.750
This was about all I could ask

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:52.700
and this was all Adachi
was able to say right now.

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:55.160
Adachi.

00:20:56.290 --> 00:20:59.120
You are walking me all the way home, right?

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:04.370
Yeah, that was my intention.

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:15.830
Look at me! I'm a plane! Vroom!

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:22.450
The slight elation that I felt
had given me wings.

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:32.040
I wonder how many steps it'll take
before embarrassment sets in.

00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:07.700
So, what's Adachi like?

00:23:07.700 --> 00:23:10.410
What is she like? Um, normal?

00:23:10.410 --> 00:23:13.370
That explains nothing,
my dear Shimamura.

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:18.250
I don't know how much I should tell you.

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:23.540
Adachi likes water
and usually drinks mineral water.

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:26.250
She doesn't seem to care about brands.

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:29.870
I see. So Adachi is a Namekian.

00:23:29.870 --> 00:23:33.620
I haven't seen her regrow
any limbs yet, though. Also...

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:35.870
Anything biting?

00:23:35.870 --> 00:23:39.750
Shukoh... Shukoh...

00:23:46.450 --> 00:23:49.950
The spacesuit was so white that it just
compounded their awkward presence.

00:23:49.950 --> 00:23:52.160
Suddenly, a small astronaut stood before me.

00:23:52.160 --> 00:23:54.580
"Episode 1: Playing Ping-Pong in Our Uniforms"

00:23:52.160 --> 00:23:54.580
Suddenly, a small astronaut stood before me.

00:23:54.580 --> 00:23:57.870
"Episode 1: Playing Ping-Pong in Our Uniforms"

00:23:57.870 --> 00:24:00.450
"Next Time: 'Adachi Question'"

00:23:57.870 --> 00:24:00.450
Adashimapedia: Ping-Pong!

00:24:00.450 --> 00:24:02.250
"Next Time: 'Adachi Question'"

00:24:00.450 --> 00:24:02.250
Explain the difference between
table tennis and ping-pong.

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:04.620
"Next Time: 'Adachi Question'"

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:04.620
When you're playing seriously,
it's table tennis. Ping-pong is just for fun.

00:24:04.620 --> 00:24:06.660
--But what about when you play
ping-pong seriously?
--Then it's table tennis.

00:24:06.660 --> 00:24:08.830
--But what about table tennis for fun?
--Then it's just ping-pong!

00:24:08.830 --> 00:24:10.910
--Ping-pong is but table tennis.
--Huh?

00:24:10.910 --> 00:24:12.660
I tried to sound philosophical.
